WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.640
It's five in the morning,
Priya's second week on the farm,

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.640
and she's got a question.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.960
Jack's busy in the shed.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.500
She asks the farm helper on her phone.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.420
It answers from the farm's
own equipment list.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.120
Take the key off the board,
hang the red tag, tell Jack.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.840
And it shows her where that
came from, so she can check.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.720
A helper is an AI assistant

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:29.060
you load with your own farm
documents and a few standing rules.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.120
Answer only from the documents.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.100
Say where the answer came from.
Say when something's missing.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.420
Here's the catch.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.080
The handbook says visitors
sign in at the dairy office.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.260
This week's jobs list
says the implement shed.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.700
Nobody spotted it.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.740
Ask the helper and it
picks one, sounds sure,

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.900
and the vet ends up
waiting at the wrong shed.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.680
So before anyone relies on
it, test three questions.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.440
One the documents answer.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.040
One they don't, like
a withholding period,

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.440
where it has to say it isn't there.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.880
And one where two documents disagree,

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.580
where it should show both
and send you to the boss.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.100
The jobs list changes every week,

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.940
so run the same three questions
every time a document changes.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:24.300
Then hand it to the team.
